{title: 296 - Lord, I'm Coming Home}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #296 • LORD IM COMING HOME • 13.13.11.12}
{lyricist: William J. Kirkpatrick}
{composer: William J. Kirkpatrick}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 296}
{meta: tune LORD IM COMING HOME}
{meta: meter 13.13.11.12}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]I've wandered far away from God, Now I'm coming home;
[Gdim]The paths [Cm/G]of [Ab]sin too long I've trod; Lord, I'm coming home.
[Ab]Coming home, coming [Gdim]home Never more [Ab]to roam;
[Ab]Open wide Thine arms of love; [Db/Ab]Lord [Ab]I'm coming home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]Coming home, [Gdim]coming home
[Ab]Never more to roam;
[Ab/Eb]Open wide Thine arms of [Gdim]love;
[Ab]Lord I'm coming home.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]I've wasted many precious years,
[Gdim]Now [Ab]I'm coming home;
[Ab]I now repent [Gdim]with bitter [Ab]tears;
[Ab]Lord, I'm coming home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]I'm tired of sin and straying Lord,
[Gdim]Now [Ab]I'm coming home;
[Ab]I'll trust thy love [Gdim]belive thy [Ab]word;
[Ab]Lord I'm coming home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Ab]My only hope, my only plea,
[Gdim]Now [Ab]I'm coming home;
[Ab]That Jesus died, [Gdim]and died for [Ab]me;
[Ab]Lord I'm coming home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Ab]I need His cleansing blood I know,
[Gdim]Now [Ab]I'm coming home;
[Ab]O wash me whiter [Gdim]than the [Ab]snow;
[Ab]Lord I'm coming home.
{end_of_verse}
